      "problem": "How many pairs of like terms are in the expression $a+2b+3-10b-9-8a?$",
      "worked_solution": "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(a)+(2b)+(3)+(-10b)+(-9)+(-8a).\n$$\n\nThere are three pairs of like terms:\n\n- $a$ and $-8a$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $a.$\n\n- $2b$ and $-10b$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $b.$\n\n- $3$ and $-9$ are like terms because they both contain no variable.",
